<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Anthony Albanese</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. <a href="/years/1963">1963</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Anthony Albanese is an Australian politician who became prime minister in May 2022 at the head of a Labor government. Member of parliament for the Sydney seat of Grayndler since 1996, he held ministerial posts in the Rudd and Gillard governments and became Labor leader in 2019. His government was re-elected with an enlarged majority in May 2025.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/anthony-albanese.jpg" alt="Anthony Albanese" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Australian Government · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Anthony_Albanese_portrait_(re-crop).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
